  "editorial": "The titles students and the Common App activities section actually use, per activity kind, each mapped to the role tier the model reads (depth.md \"What the student enters\": member took part, officer a named role, leader ran it). A title is a level within a tier, not a tier of its own: on a sports team, Varsity is still member tier (everyone on the roster is a member; being varsity is a level of play, not a role), while Captain and Co-captain are leader because the team follows them. A club's elected or appointed posts split the same way: Secretary, Treasurer, Vice President, and Committee chair run a piece of the club (officer); President and Founder run the whole thing (leader). Researched from the Common App's own activities guidance and how students commonly describe each kind.",
